<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103788" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τηλαυγ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆλε, αὐγή</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>far-shining, far-beaming</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόσωπον</span>, of the sun, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Hom.</u>
				31.13
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἵματα</span>, of the moon,
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				32.8
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάος, φέγγος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				3.75
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			), <i><span class="en">
				<u>N.</u>
				3.64
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκτίς, ἀκτίνων σέλας</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				1092
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				1711
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέφανοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					2.6
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόσωπον θέμεν τ</span>. to make
			it <i>beam from afar</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>O.</u>
				6.4
			</span></i>: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. νοῦς</span>
			<i>luminous</i> meaning, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Th.</u>
				30
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σαφεῖς καὶ τ. αἰτίαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					5.174d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέξεις ἐπὶ τὸ -έστερον ἀχθεῖσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Erot.
					<u>Prooem.</u>
				</span></i>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of distant objects,
				<i>far-seen, conspicuous</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοπιή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					550
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κορυφά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Pae.</u>
					7.12
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φᾶρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					16.5
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄχθος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					524
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); of leprosy, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Le.</u>
				13.4
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>far-seeing</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴσθησις,
			ψυχή</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				17
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				22
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			). Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-γῶς, τηλαυγέστερον ὁρᾶν</span> to see
				<i>more clearly</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				1.50
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				17.1.30
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.540
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Marc.</u>
				8.25
			</span></i>.--Poet. word, used in late Prose: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δηλαυγῶς</span> seems to be a different word.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
